<title>GERMANY: New telecoms venture to be called Mannesmann Arcor.</title>
<headline>New telecoms venture to be called Mannesmann Arcor.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The new name of the telecommunications joint venture between Mannesmann, Deutsche Bahn AG (German railways) and the AT&amp;T/Unisource group is Mannesmann Arcor AG and Co, company officials said.</p>
<p>The joint venture, announced last summer, had hitherto retained the name of Deutsche Bahn's telecommunications network, DBKom.</p>
<p>Officials said Arcor stands for &quot;the golden bridge to our customers&quot;.</p>
<p>Arcor hopes to become the second most important telecomunications company in Germany next to Deutsche Telekom AG.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom +49-228-2609760</p>
